<abstract xml:lang="zh"><p>轻度污染的生活污水（即灰水）回用被视为减轻城市供水和排水系统负荷的途径之一。本简报介绍了在一个由三栋多户住宅楼（412 名居民）组成的住宅街区中灰水处理系统试运行的结果。来自淋浴和洗脸盆的灰水在一套紧凑型装置中进行处理，该装置包括机械过滤、膜生物反应器和紫外线消毒，处理后的水用于冲厕和周边场地绿化灌溉。在 12 个月内，每日记录水量，每周监测处理后水质。回用使饮用水消耗量平均减少 27%，夏季月份因灌溉需求减少幅度最高可达 34%。处理后的水在浊度、生化需氧量和微生物指标方面始终符合非饮用供水标准。单位运行成本约为每立方米 38 卢布，按现行水价估算的投资回收期为 9～11 年。居民调查显示，在水无异味、无变色的前提下，居民对该技术的接受度很高（82% 给予正面评价）。我们得出结论：灰水回用系统值得纳入新建住宅开发项目。</p></abstract>
<trans-abstract xml:lang="en"><p>The reuse of lightly polluted domestic wastewater, or greywater, is regarded as one way to reduce the load on urban water supply and sewerage systems. This short communication presents the results of a pilot operation of a greywater treatment system in a residential block of three multi-apartment buildings (412 residents). Greywater from showers and washbasins was treated in a compact unit comprising mechanical filtration, a membrane bioreactor and ultraviolet disinfection, and then supplied for toilet flushing and irrigation of the surrounding grounds. Over 12 months, volumes were recorded daily and the quality of treated water was monitored weekly. Reuse reduced potable water consumption by 27% on average and by up to 34% in summer months owing to irrigation. Treated water consistently met the standards for non-potable water supply in terms of turbidity, biochemical oxygen demand and microbiological indicators. Specific operating costs were about 38 roubles per cubic metre, and the payback period at current tariffs is estimated at 9–11 years. A survey of residents showed a high level of acceptance of the technology (82% positive ratings), provided the water had no odour or discolouration. We conclude that greywater reuse systems are worth including in new residential development projects.</p></trans-abstract>
